## 4. ORIGINAL BLUR GAMEPLAY REFERENCE

Understand the essential characteristics of Blur before implementing the game.

Blur combines traditional arcade racing with combat-oriented collectible power-ups.

Players drive around detailed racing circuits, collect energy-based abilities, attack opponents, defend against incoming attacks, repair vehicle damage, and use speed boosts.

Races are not determined only by vehicle speed. Strategy, power-up selection, positioning, defensive timing, and driving skill are equally important.

Preserve these gameplay pillars:

1. High-speed driving.
2. Competitive racing.
3. Tactical power-up combat.
4. Accessible but skill-based vehicle handling.
5. Real-time defensive counterplay.
6. Vehicle damage and recovery.
7. Dynamic race positions.
8. Competitive online multiplayer.
9. Vehicle progression.
10. Visually impressive energy effects.

Do not turn the game into a simulator, endless runner, top-down racing game, kart racing game, or basic 2D driving application.

